<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44029" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sētănĭa</span></b> ,
		ae, f., and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sētănĭum</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-on</span></b> ), i,
		n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σητανία</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σητάνιον</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The name of a kind of medlar</i>: setania, 
			<i><span class="en">Plin. 15,
				20, 22, § 84</span></i>.—Also in the <i>neutr. subst.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non possunt militares pueri setania educier,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Truc. 5, 16</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Setania, <i>a kind of onion</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 19,
				6, 32, § 102</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b> Setanion, <i>a kind of
				bulb</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 19, 5, 30, §
		95</span></i>.</div>
